From: MoveCertificate contributors
Subject: [PATCH] gralloc: query mapper metadata before legacy format rejection

P010 allocation succeeds on PGKM10 but the common AHB properties query fails
before the modern mapper backend is called. A standalone mapper query reads
valid linear P010 and AFBC YUV metadata on this device. Preserve the existing
legacy fallback when mapper lookup fails; do not invent layouts or formats.
This addresses query ordering only. Packed AFBC YUV format support and FD
selection require separate validation.

--- a/src/util/u_gralloc/u_gralloc_fallback.c
+++ b/src/util/u_gralloc/u_gralloc_fallback.c
@@ -586,6 +586,14 @@
    if (hnd->handle->numFds == 0)
       return -EINVAL;
 
+   /* Standard mapper metadata covers formats such as P010 which the old
+    * gralloc0 HAL format table cannot represent. Query it before legacy
+    * conversion or lock_ycbcr can reject a valid native buffer.
+    */
+   int stable_ret = panvk_v19_query_mapper(hnd->handle, out);
+   if (stable_ret == 0)
+      return 0;
+
    if (is_hal_format_yuv(hnd->hal_format)) {
       int ret = fallback_gralloc_get_yuv_info(gralloc, hnd, out);
       /*
@@ -635,7 +643,6 @@
 
 
 
-   int stable_ret = panvk_v19_query_mapper(hnd->handle, out);
    if (stable_ret != 0) {
       mesa_logw("[P0A-V19-FULLPLANE] complete metadata unavailable rc=%d; refusing guessed layout",
                 stable_ret);
